.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBHistogramRangeSlider\fR: a histogram over a range slider that edit \fBone\fR range. Pressing a bar picks that bin's range, dragging a thumb moves the ends, and the bars inside the range are accented.
.PP
It is a \fBComposedComponent\fR: two parts (a minimal \fBBarChart::histogram\fR and a \fBrange_slider\fR), one shared range, one \fBon_change\fR, and one rule (\fBlo <= hi\fR). The bounds of the slider are the histogram's own, so there is nothing to keep in step. The gallery's Composed component page shows how it is defined.
.PP
.nf
.RS
HistogramRangeSlider::new(&self.bpm, self.range, Msg::Range).step(1.0)
.RE
.fi
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B HistogramRangeSlider::new(histogram: impl Into<Cow<'a, Histogram>>, range: (f32, f32), on_change: impl Fn((f32, f32)) \-> M + 'a)
\fBhistogram\fR is borrowed (\fB&hist\fR) or owned (\fBHistogram::from_counts(..)\fR built in the view, for one that depends on a filter). \fBrange\fR is the chosen \fB(lo, hi)\fR within its \fBmin..max\fR; \fBon_change\fR gets the next range from whichever part the user touched.
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.step(step: f32)
How far a thumb moves at a time, and the least the thumbs may be apart. Without one the thumbs move freely.
.TP
.B \&.height(px: f32)
The height of the bars (default 48).
.TP
.B \&.full(full: bool)
With axes, gridlines, tooltip and hover on the bars, in the series color (default bare).
